# Four Knocks: a horror game for AerOS
# Run it with:
#     knocks
#
# CONTENT WARNING: darkness, sudden loud noises, frightening images, and death and loss.
# Play it with headphones: what you hear tells you where things are.
#
# Controls:
#     W / S, Up / Down     - walk forwards and backwards
#     A / D                - step sideways
#     Left / Right, mouse  - turn (the mouse also looks up and down; in QEMU click the window
#                            first, and Ctrl+Alt+G lets go)
#     Shift (held)         - run: quicker, and loud
#     C or Ctrl (held)     - creep: slow, and almost silent
#     Space (held)         - hold your breath
#     E, Enter, left click - use what is in front of you: read, take, open, answer
#     F, right click       - your flashlight on or off
#     Tab (held)           - what you are doing, and what you carry
#     Escape               - pause (and from there, quit)
#
# THE STORY
#
#   October 1989. Your father, Martin Venn, was the engineer at the Corvid Hill Deep
#   Observatory: a station on a lonely hill, built over a borehole four kilometres deep, to
#   listen to the earth. In March 1986 he vanished with the ten other people who worked there.
#   The doors were found chained from the inside, and the building empty.
#
#   Last night your answering machine played you a message in his voice: come down, and
#   bring my key. You still have it.
#
#   It is told by what you find: notes, tapes, a telephone, the places themselves. In short
#   (spoilers): in 1986 the observatory heard four knocks from the bottom of the hole, and
#   answered them. What came up the hole is blind, finds people by the sounds they make, and
#   copies what it hears, voices most of all. Martin trapped it on the lower level by cutting
#   the lift's power; it has been calling up the telephone line ever since. There are two
#   endings.
#
# HOW IT WORKS, for anyone who wants to build on it
#
#   It is the ray caster from Maze 3D (packages/maze3d.aer, which explains it step by step):
#   the walls, floor and ceiling are pictures drawn with imgcol and imgrow, and imglight
#   shines your flashlight on them, black outside its beam. What is new here:
#
#   - The view is letterboxed (black bars above and below, where the subtitles and the
#     words go), like a film, and its proportions come from the screen's width (PROJ).
#   - The thing and the furniture are sprites drawn with imgcol(..., true): strips of a
#     picture with see-through parts, lit by the flashlight like the walls, so the thing is
#     only there when your beam is on it. They are 3D models, rendered from 5 sides by
#     tools/make_knocks_sprites.py (and mirrored for the other 3).
#   - Sounds have a place: splay's pan puts each on the left or right, and svol moves it as
#     you turn. The thing's footsteps get quieter the further away it is, counted along the
#     corridors (the "step map", see steps_from), so you hear it round corners, not through
#     walls.
#   - The thing hunts by ear. Every frame you make a noise (see noise_now): none standing,
#     a little creeping, more walking, a lot running. If it is that many steps away or
#     fewer, it hears you, and goes to where it heard you. If you're close enough, it runs.
#   - imglight's ambient light shows everything for a moment in a flash of lightning; gtint
#     fades the picture and flashes it red; gnoise is the static you see when it is near.
#   - The sounds and pictures are made by tools/make_knocks_sounds.py,
#     tools/make_knocks_textures.py and tools/make_knocks_sprites.py, and loaded from the
#     game's folder (/apps/knocks/).
#
#   For testing: "knocks demo" plays itself from start to end (the thing can't catch it;
#   "knocks demo 2" from level B2, and "knocks demo 2 leave" to the other ending), printing
#   what it does,
#   "knocks start 2" (or 3) starts on that level, and "knocks safe" plays with a harmless
#   thing. Progress is saved in /apps/knocks/save.txt when you reach each level.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The map
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One grid holds all three levels: the observatory's ground floor (top left), the level
# below it, B2 (the bottom half), and the casing round the borehole (top right). The lift and
# the stairs move you between them. Each letter is a square:
#
#   .  floor                      D  wooden door      M  steel door (both open with E)
#   #  wallpaper  W  window       P  wood panels      Q  wallpaper with tally marks
#   C  concrete   K  pipes        T  tiles            S  concrete, QUIET scratched on it
#   A  tape shelves               R  rock             O  the borehole's casing
#   B  the front doors            L  the lift         Z  the stairs down
#   G  the generator              V  the power board  H  the charge console   Y  the ladder

