# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The words: notes, and the lines of the recordings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A note is its heading, then its words (\n starts a new paragraph). They are wrapped to fit.

let NOTES = [
    nil,
    ["SIGNING IN BOOK, 14 MARCH 1986", "R. ASKEW (Director)     in 07:50     out\nM. VENN (Engineer)      in 07:55     out\nJ. PELL (Technician)    in 08:10     out\nS. OKAFOR (Geophysics)  in 08:12     out\n... and seven more names.\n\nNobody signed out.\n\nAt the bottom of the page, in pencil, pressed so hard it tore the paper:\nDON'T ANSWER IT"],
    ["BOREHOLE CH-1: LOG", "4,120 metres deep. Eight geophones (listening sensors) hang in it, numbered from the bottom up: number 1 at 4,000 metres, number 8 just under the surface.\n\n2 Feb 1986. A signal on geophone 1. Four sharp knocks, 0.7 seconds apart. Then nothing for eleven minutes. Then four more. Not an earthquake. Not the drill.\n\nDr Askew wants us to answer it with the thumper. - S. Okafor"],
    ["BOREHOLE CH-1: LOG (CONTINUED)", "3 Feb. We sent four knocks down the hole. Four came back within the hour.\n\n5 Feb. It sent ours back. Not four knocks: OUR four knocks. The thumper's own sound, with the fault in the third strike.\n\n19 Feb. Geophone 2 now. Louder.\n\n28 Feb. Geophone 3. Martin says the hole is a throat, and we have been shouting down it. - S.O."],
    ["MEMO FROM THE DIRECTOR", "From today nobody is to use the intercom, or the telephones to B2.\n\nWhatever is on those lines is not the switchboard.\n\nAnd if you hear me call you from somewhere I could not be, do not come. - R. Askew"],
    ["A NOTE UNDER A PILLOW", "It heard me through the intercom. I was on the phone to my sister and I said her name, and that night it said her name back to me, through the wall by my bunk. In my voice.\n\nIt doesn't need to see. It listens.\n\nDon't talk near the speakers. Don't talk at all. - Jonah"],
    ["PINNED BY THE KETTLE", "Since they bricked up the stairs to B2, the lift is the only way down or up. Martin has the only key. He says it can't climb. It can only call.\n\nSo nobody answers, and nobody goes down. We wait for the road to clear. - J.P."],
    ["EMERGENCY GENERATOR", "Powers: the lift, the emergency lights.\n\nTo start: fit fuse F2 in the holder at the bottom, then press START.\n\nSpare fuses are kept in the dormitory lockers."],
    ["IN YOUR FATHER'S HANDWRITING", "If you are reading this, something brought you down here. I cut the lift's power from below so that it could never come up.\n\nIt is blind. It finds you by the sounds you make.\nWalk slowly (hold C). Never run unless it has already heard you.\nIf it comes close, stand still, and hold your breath (hold SPACE).\n\n- M. Venn"],
    ["TAPE ARCHIVE: INDEX CARD", "Reel 0217. FOUR KNOCKS (ORIGINAL). Geophone 1, 2 Feb 1986. Shelf C, bottom.\n\nIn red pen: the only recording of its own knock, not ours. Keep it safe. - M."],
    ["DR ASKEW'S DESK", "The survey charges: four of them, in the casing at the foot of the stairs, laid for the deep seismic shoot we never made. Enough to bring the hole down, and everything near it.\n\nThe arming key is in my desk. The console is by the casing.\n\nMartin thinks that if we play it its own knock, it will come to the sound. Then we set them off. Someone has to be down there to do it. - R.A."],
    ["SCRATCHED ON THE MIRROR", "Sara has been gone four days.\n\nFor two days after, I heard her calling me from the store room. I knew it wasn't her. I nearly went anyway. - J."],
    ["B2 POWER BOARD", "Restores: the lift, the stair door to the casing, the casing's speakers.\n\nWARNING: the board is LOUD when thrown."],
    ["THE STORE: A LIST", "Food: 3 days. Water. Batteries: 6. Rope.\n\nMartin has gone to get the key from Ruth's desk, and then down to the casing with the tape. He told us to stay here and keep quiet.\n\nIf he doesn't come back, take the lift up when the power's on. Don't look for him. - J.P."],
    ["YOUR FATHER'S THINGS", "His coat, folded. His headphones. A note under them:\n\nCouldn't reach Ruth's desk for the key. It was between me and it. So I've led it down here instead, to keep it busy as long as I can.\n\nIf anyone finds this: the tape in the slot, then turn the key. The hatch over the ladder opens when the charges arm. You'll have a minute.\n\nIt's coming. I can hear it on the stairs. - M."]
]

